.TH "SERIALPORT.FORGET" "3JS" "April 25, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
SerialPort.forget \- SerialPort: forget() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Dedicated Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]SerialPort.forget()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]SerialPort\f[R] interface returns a \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that
resolves when access to the serial port is revoked.
.SH DESCRIPTION
A website can clean up permissions to access a serial port it is no
longer interested in retaining by calling
\f[CR]SerialPort.forget()\f[R].
Calling this \(lqforgets\(rq the device, resetting any previously\-set
permissions so the calling site can no longer communicate with the port.
.PP
For example, for an educational web application used on a shared
computer with many devices, a large number of accumulated
user\-generated permissions creates a poor user experience.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
forget()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
A \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that resolves with \f[CR]undefined\f[R] once the
connection is revoked.
